# Backend tests

Uses Node's built-in test runner (`node:test`). Run all of them with:

    npm test

(equivalent to `node --test`, run from the `server/` directory)

## Files

### mapping.test.js
Pure unit tests for `mapPageToNewsEvent` in `services/notions.js` — the function that
turns a raw Notion page into the JSON shape returned by `/api/news-events`. No network
calls; every Notion property type (title, rich_text, select, multi_select, date,
checkbox, url, place) is tested against both a populated value and its missing/empty
edge case, using hand-built fixture pages.

### slug.test.js
Pure unit tests for `slugify` and `resolveSlugs` in `services/notions.js` — the pass
that gives every published item a URL even when the Notion `Slug` property is left
blank. Covers accent stripping, punctuation collapsing, precedence of an explicit Slug
over a derived one, page-id disambiguation when two titles collide, and that the input
items are not mutated. No network calls.

### content.test.js
Pure unit tests for `mapBlock` and `collectImages` in `services/notions.js` — the pass
that turns the Notion page body behind each item into the content nodes the article
dialog renders. Covers every supported block type (paragraphs, headings, lists,
quotes, callouts, toggles, images, dividers), rich-text annotations and links, both
Notion-hosted and external image URLs, that unsupported types and empty paragraphs are
dropped, and that the flat image list leads with the featured image and de-duplicates.
No network calls.

### config.test.js
Confirms `getPublishedNewsEvents()` rejects with a clear, actionable error when
`NOTION_API_KEY` or `NOTION_DATABASE_ID` isn't set, instead of failing with a raw
Notion SDK error. No network calls. Must not run in the same process as a test that
successfully resolves the data source id (that gets cached at module scope) — this is
safe because `node --test` runs each test file in its own process.

### query.test.js
Integration tests that call the real Notion database configured in `server/.env`:
checks the shape/types of every returned field, that `Status` is always `Published`,
that `Published Date` is never in the future, that Slugs are unique, that results are
sorted newest-first, and both branches of `getPublishedNewsEventBySlug` (found and
not-found). Skips (not fails) with a clear message if `NOTION_API_KEY` /
`NOTION_DATABASE_ID` aren't set. Because it hits the live API, it's the slowest file
and will fail if the integration's token or database access changes.
